I think your best bet would have been to zap it with the wand of fire, 
which does most damage (which is however not possible anymore after you 
cancelled your inventory :-) ).  If you had survived one more turn, that 
should have been sufficient, IMO.

Of course, you *should* have completely identified your wand called 
"Engr_vanishes" before by zapping it at an object you know to be blessed 
or cursed.  If nothing happens, it is make invisible, if the object gets 
uncursed, cancellation, if the object disappears, teleport. (In slashem, 
you can take any object, because invisibility will render the object 
invisible.  If you don't have see invisible, you must go feel for it to 
make sure the difference between teleport and make invisible.)  Even if 
you had no cursed or blessed object, you could have found out whether it 
is teleport or not, in which case you would have known whether to zap it 
at yourself or at the vortex.  (Make invisible would of course not have 
saved you, so in that case, fire would still have been your best bet.)
